{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1556545195,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MzgzMjExODA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3361","origin":"github"},"title":"we might need to reconsider approach for text2git","message":"Attn @joeyh \nATM we are using \n```\n* annex.largefiles=(not(mimetype=text/*))\n```\nbut as we have recently discovered ([git-annex bug report](http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/manages_to_incorrectly_add_to_annex_instead_of_git_based_on___34__mimetype__34___-_we_cannot_figure_it_out_why/#comment-e0fec0da5dec5241db65324dcba2d3be)), it has stopped working for .json files since `file/libmagic` acquired additional powers to annotate them as `application/json`.\n\n# Possible \"proper\" solutions\n\n[Discussion on the `file` mailing list](https://mailman.astron.com/pipermail/file/2019-April/000106.html) brought following,\n- We might want to consider using instead `encoding` not `type`. So we could then say:\n```\n* annex.largefiles=(mimeencoding=binary)\n```\nwhich is kinda neat IMHO!  But that would require adding support for that to git-annex\n- We could (potentially, since there is [a bug in file/libmagic forbidding it](https://bugs.astron.com/view.php?id=77)) use `-k, --keep-going` flag and get all entries for each file to be matched.  But that would also require changes to git-annex and possibly more substantial since probably it was not coded to associate multiple mime types per file\n\nThere is also `-e json` which could be added to `file` call to exclude detection of json, but if anything (again, changed in annex) it would be a dirty hack/workaround, nothing really to rely upon.\n\n# Temporary workaround\nSo I guess, in the short run, we should just add explicit \n```\n*.json annex.largefiles=nothing\n```\nor alike (limit by size in addition).\n\nAny other ideas?","files":null}]}